1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,951
What would actually happen to you if you fell into a black hole?

2
00:00:02,951 --> 00:00:07,337
As you drift closer in your spacesuit, spacetime begins to warp violently.

3
00:00:07,337 --> 00:00:13,356
At the Photon Sphere, gravity bends light into circles, allowing you to see the back of your own head.

4
00:00:13,356 --> 00:00:15,578
Next, you cross the Event Horizon.

5
00:00:15,578 --> 00:00:17,928
This is the ultimate point of no return.

6
00:00:17,928 --> 00:00:19,594
Not even light can escape.

7
00:00:19,594 --> 00:00:22,986
Here, gravitational time dilation reaches extremes.

8
00:00:22,986 --> 00:00:27,824
Looking backward, you see the entire future of the universe speed by in seconds.

9
00:00:27,824 --> 00:00:30,902
Meanwhile, tidal forces become astronomical.

10
00:00:30,902 --> 00:00:34,953
The gravity pulling your feet is billions of times stronger than at your head.

11
00:00:34,953 --> 00:00:41,145
This stretches your body into a thin string of atoms, a cosmic process called spaghettification.

12
00:00:41,145 --> 00:00:46,817
Finally, you crush into the singularity, where infinite gravity breaks the laws of physics.

13
00:00:46,817 --> 00:00:48,541
Would you dare explore a black hole?

14
00:00:48,541 --> 00:00:49,849
Tell us in the comments.

